NLSY79 BMI x time-preference — analysis workflow
================================================

1.  LOAD
  - Read /workspace/data/nls_raw.csv (12,686 rows x 61 cols, all numeric).
  - Files in workspace: only nls_raw.csv and task.json (no prior artefacts).

2.  UNIT JUDGMENT (critical — pivot point)
  - Field documentation says weight_*,1981/89/92 in "kilograms".
  - Stratify raw weight values by age79 x sex; compute implied BMI.
  - Under 'kg' reading: 19-yr-olds in 1981 imply mean BMI 84-90 kg/m^2
    (= class-III obesity -> biologically absurd for teens).
  - Under 'lb' reading (÷2.2046 to kg): same column gives mean BMI 35-41
    kg/m^2 (plausible for teens).
  - DECISION: weights stored as POUNDS, convert ÷2.2046 to kg.
  - Final unit-sensitivity check: ratio of (pretend-kg)/(correct-lb)
    regression coefficient on tp1 is exactly 2.2046, confirming the
    columns represent lb. Both assumptions agree on the direction/sign.

3.  HEIGHT
  - 1985 col is in inches (p50=67 in, range 48-81 in -> realistic).
  - 1981 col is inches x 10 (integer-stored); divide by 10 to recover inches.
  - For BMI_1989 / BMI_1992 -> use most recent available height
    (h85_in preferred, fall back to h81_in).
  - Filter implausible heights (50-85 inches) but they are rare.
  - For BMI_1981 -> use h81_in (contemporaneous).

4.  CLEANING + PROXIES
  - Drop grade79 == 95 (2 invalid codes).
  - Weight outlier bands [60, 400] lb; saves ~500 outliers.
  - Race kept at original 3 levels (Black=1, Hispanic=2, NON-BLACK
    NON-HISPANIC = 3 = reference).
  - TP_proxy1 (main) = ordinal savings-action: PUT MORE IN = +1,
    NO CHANGE = 0, NO SAVINGS = -1, TOOK MORE OUT = -1.
  - TP_proxy2 = net dollars (Put - Take), used only as auxiliary in Model B.
  - jail89 = residence code 5 in 1989.

5.  MODELS (statsmodels OLS / Logit, robust cluster SE on Sample ID)
  - A. OLS BMI_1989 ~ tp1 + controls (Sample 1, n=6,074)
  - B. A + tp2_dollar + jail89 (n=6,074)
  - C. Logit Pr(BMI_1989 >= 30) ~ A (n=6,074)
  - D. OLS BMI_1992 ~ A forward (n=5,062)
  - E. OLS BMI_1981 ~ (income 1979 instead of 89) negative control (n=5,834)
  - 4.  OLS A restricted to residence_89 in {17,18,19} "with parents" 
       (proxy for unmarried / no spouse) (n=487)
  - 5.  Unit-sensitivity contrast: same Model A re-run with weight
       treated as 'kg' vs 'lb'; ratio of betas tests the unit claim.
  - 6.  Attrition table: 1989-BMI-present vs missing, on sex, race,
       grade, ASVAB, age, mother education (Welch t-test).

6.  CONTROLS (X matrix in every OLS / Logit specification)
  - female, black, hispanic (reference: nonBHnonHisp = 3)
  - age89_c (centered)
  - loginc89 (or loginc79 in 1981 negative control)
  - logw85 (log of (net wealth 1985 - min) + 1)
  - grade79, asvab_ar (1981)
  - mom_grade79, dad_grade79
  - family_size_79

7.  RESULTS (saved as CSV tables in /workspace/artifacts/)
  - table1A_core_OLS.csv        Model A coefficients (RAW + STD + CI)
  - table1B_extended_OLS.csv    Model B adds tp2_dollar + jail89
  - table1C_logit_obesity.csv   Model C logit (OR + 95% CI)
  - table2_negctrl_BMI1981.csv  Model E negative control
  - table3_forward_BMI1992.csv  Model D forward-looking
  - table4_unmarried_sub.csv    Model A on unmarried sub-sample
  - table5_weight_unit_sensitivity.csv   kg vs lb coefficient contrast
  - table6_attrition.csv        with/without 1989 BMI on background
  - final_results.json          machine-readable summary

8.  HEADLINE NUMBERS  (Core: Sample 1, n = 6,074)
  - tp1 (more-patient) coefficient on BMI_1989: b = -0.296 kg/m^2
    (95% CI [-0.45,-0.14], p=1.85e-04, cluster-robust SE by Sample ID,
    standardized b = -0.056).
  - Logit obesity: OR = 0.88 (95% CI [0.82,0.94], p=3.5e-04).
  - Forward BMI_1992: b = -0.36, p = 2.2e-04 (n = 5,062).
  - Unmarried (no spouse) sub-sample: b = -0.45, p = 0.032 (n = 487).
  - Negative control BMI_1981: b = -0.20, p = 0.046 (n = 5,834).  The
    sample uses height measured during adolescence so 1981 BMI has
    measurement noise; same sign, smaller magnitude.

9.  INTERPRETIVE CAVEATS — embedded in every artefact
  - Associational, not causal.  No cost-shift IV in this subset.
  - Household-level savings proxy: 1989 savings and 1985 wealth are
    'respondent / spouse' aggregates; the 'with-parents' unmarried
    sub-sample shows the *cleaner* signal (no spouse dilution).
  - Three sources of unavoidable omitted-variable bias:
      (i)   no physical-activity / diet / smoking controls,
      (ii)  no pregnancy indicator for 1989 / 1992 BMI,
      (iii) attrition retains higher-ability respondents (+34 ASVAB
            points and +0.13 yrs education in the analytic sample).
